game, blending exploration and cinematic cutscenes with puzzle elements</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>A Tragic Tale of Family</strong> <br>A heart-wrenching story about the lengths we can go to protect the ones we love</p></li></ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Art Style and Atmosphere</strong> <br>A haunting soundtrack and hand-crafted pixel art create an eerie, immersive, fully voiced gameplay experience</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Narrative Focused</strong><br>Uncover a rich storyline that paints the lives of the people who lived in Deer Creek, their relationships and secrets     <br>  </p></li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Technical Features</strong>:</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>An Accessible, Narrative-driven Point-and-Click Adventure Game</strong><br>A simple single-click interface makes the game easy for anyone to play  </p></li></ul>", "short_description": "A cinematic point-and-click adventure where you step into the shoes of photographer Charlotte Gray as she explores the abandoned camp of Deer Creek and uncovers the tragedy that befell the camp and its people.", "supported_languages": "English<strong>*</strong><br><strong>*</strong>languages with full audio support", "reviews": "“I very much enjoyed my few hours spent in this ghost town, and my heart fell when I had to leave, wanting to find out more about its history and the people who once lived there, and the events that followed the tragedy that befell them.”<br>85/100 – Adventure Game Hotspot<br><br>“The Tragedy at Deer Creek is a well crafted, atmospheric mystery that recaptures the best of classic point and click adventure gaming without having to rely on nostalgia as driving factor.”<br>9.5/10 – Dad with a Deck<br><br>“The Tragedy at Deer Creek deserves its moment in the spotlight. A cinematic point-and-click adventure about exploring an abandoned logging camp, it’s a game that exudes atmospher